@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed — Create link, verify viewer and admit exact retrieval
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Owner
participant Sharing as S
participant "Current authority / verifier" as A
participant "Presentation / Files contracts" as F
actor Viewer
Owner -> S : explicit exact link/content configuration
S -> A : current owner management scope
S -> F : intended publication / exact usable reference evidence
S -> S : guarded configuration + protected verifier reference + command result
S --> Owner : actual bounded management outcome
Viewer -> S : intended link + supplied password proof
S -> A : current eligibility and actual verification / abuse controls
alt proof valid and link currently eligible
 S -> S : establish bounded viewer context tied to current generation
 Viewer -> S : exact web / PDF / language request
 S -> S : recheck current link/context/mode/content at protected admission
 S -> F : exact permitted manifest / usable bytes and delivery protection
 F --> Viewer : controlled permitted output or safe unavailable
else denied / disabled / expired / unavailable
 S --> Viewer : safe bounded refusal; no private fallback
end
note over S,F
 Every later request, range request and cache route needs current checks.
 Early positive verification is not perpetual byte-access authority.
end note

@enduml
